        "Content": "No. 12 Cannon’s Court,  Mountcharles  F94 CD88\r\n\r\n3 Bed (all en-suite)  Town House\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSituate just off Main Street and just  5.5 km west of Donegal Town.  Constructed in 2004 and extending to 137.05 sq.m (1475 sq.ft.).  Mountcharles Beach is within 1 km\r\n\r\nGround Floor.\tLiving Room,  Fitted Kitchen with Dining Area,  W.C.;\r\nFirst Floor.\t\t2 No. Bedrooms (both en-suite)\r\nSecond Floor.\t1 No. Large Bedroom (en-suite)\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHallway\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLiving Room\t\t\t4.47 m.  x  4.10 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tlaminated floor,  fireplace;  opening to -\r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nKitchen\t\t\t5.02 m.  x  3.84 m.\r\n\t\t\t\ttiled floor;  fitted units with integrated fridge freezer and  \t\t\t\t\tbuilt-in oven & hob;  french doors to rear \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nW.C.\t\t\t\tToilet & Wash Basin – tiled floor\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFirst Floor.\r\n\r\nBedroom No. 1\t\t4.61 m.  x  3.52 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tsemi-solid timber floor\r\n\r\n\t\tEn-suite\telectric shower, toilet and wash basin; tiled floor and around \t\t\t\tshower\r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nBedroom No. 2\t\t4.50 m.  x  3.73 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tsemi-solid timber floor\r\n\r\n\t\tEn-suite\tBath with electric shower overhead, toilet and wash basin; \t\t\t\ttiled floor and above bath\r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nSecond Floor.\r\n\r\nBedroom No. 3\t\t6.23 m.  x  3.67 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tvelox window,  carpet\r\n\r\n\t\tEn-suite\tCorner shower, toilet and wash basin\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAttic\t\t\t\tAccess via Stira Stairs and floored\r\n\r\nOil fired central heating\t\tP.V.C.  Double Glazed Windows\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nA  local link bus service connects Mountcharles to Killybegs & Donegal Town several times a day\r\n\r\nWithin Village is a Convenience Shop,  Butchers,  Fish Shop,  Post Office,  Now Doc,  2 No. Pubs,  Primary School, 2 No. Churches & St.Nauls GAA Pitch.     Mountcharles Beach is within 1 km.\r\n\r\nAnderson Auctioneers for itself and as agent for the vendor gives notice that:\r\n\r\nThese particulars are only a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees and do not constitute in whole or in part, an offer or a Contract.\r\n\r\nAny intending purchaser or lessee should satisfy themselves by inspection, searches, inquiries, and survey as to the correctness of each statement.\r\n\r\n[OR] Whilst every care has been taken in the preparation of these particulars, and they are believed to be correct, they are not warranted and intending purchasers/lessees should satisfy themselves as to the correctness of the information given.\r\n\r\nAll statements in these particulars are made on the without responsibility part of Anderson Auctioneers or the vendor \r\n\r\nNo statement in these particulars is to be relied upon as a statement or representation of fact.\r\n\r\nNeither Anderson Auctioneers nor anyone in its employment or acting on its behalf has authority to make any representation or warranty in relation to this property.\r\n\r\nNothing in these particulars shall be deemed to be a statement that the property is in good repair or condition or otherwise nor that any services or facilities are in good working order.\r\n\r\nPhotographs may show only certain parts and aspects of the property at the time when the photographs were taken and you should rely upon actual inspection.\r\n\r\nNo assumption should be made in respect of parts of the property not shown in photographs.\r\n\r\nAny areas, measurements, or distances are only approximate.\r\n\r\nAny reference to alterations or use is not intended to be a statement that any necessary planning, building regulation, listed building or any other consent has been obtained."
